      "proof_review": {
        "reviewed": true,
        "context_checked": true,
        "method": "Published author proof/core and local context fidelity screening",
        "note": "The complete Theorem3.3 constructive proof is included. M is a smooth manifold with a torsion-free affine connection, omega has fixed Pfaff rank k-1 through omega wedge (domega)^k=0 and omega wedge (domega)^(k-1) nowhere zero, and the given omega-Legendrian foliation has leafwise positive-definite symmetric covariant derivative S^nabla omega. The result is local at every point, with strictly nabla-convex functions constant on the prescribed leaves and positive smooth coefficients. The classical Pfaff-Darboux theorem is explicitly prior background; the author actually gives all of the new convexity and positivity adjustments. The unadapted corollary and Euclidean special case are not additional counted units."
      },
